#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"mappers-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map operator representations {#map-operator-representations}"
msgstr "Memetakan representasi operator {#map-operator-representations}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A **mapper** turns a [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") into a qubit operator, here a [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable). The operator itself knows nothing about qubits: it stores ladder operators on modes, and a bosonic mode holds arbitrarily many particles. Everything that makes the operator finite (how many occupation levels you keep, and how those levels are laid out on qubits) is decided when you map it.\n"
msgstr "Sebuah **mapper** mengubah [`BosonOperator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator\") menjadi operator qubit, di sini berupa [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable). Operatornya sendiri tidak tahu apa-apa soal qubit: ia menyimpan operator ladder pada mode, dan sebuah mode bosonik bisa menampung partikel dalam jumlah berapa pun. Semua yang membuat operator itu berhingga (berapa banyak level okupansi yang kamu pertahankan, dan bagaimana level-level itu ditata di qubit) ditentukan saat kamu memetakannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The library mapper [`occupation_encoding()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-library-occupation-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding\") works in the occupation (Fock) basis: level $n$ of a mode is the state with $n$ bosons. It takes the operator and a [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\"), which holds the truncation and the encoding. This guide explains what those two choices mean and what each one costs. For an end-to-end route that uses them, see [Simulate Bose-Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started); for how the transpiler applies the same choices to a whole circuit, see [Transpile bosonic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"
msgstr "Mapper pustaka [`occupation_encoding()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-library-occupation-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.library.occupation_encoding\") bekerja di basis okupansi (Fock): level $n$ dari sebuah mode adalah state dengan $n$ boson. Ia menerima operator dan sebuah [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\"), yang menyimpan pemotongan (truncation) dan encoding. Panduan ini menjelaskan apa arti kedua pilihan itu dan berapa biaya masing-masing. Untuk alur end-to-end yang memakainya, lihat [Simulasikan dinamika Bose-Hubbard dengan pilihan encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-getting-started); untuk cara Transpiler menerapkan pilihan yang sama pada seluruh Circuit, lihat [Transpile Circuit bosonik](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"truncation-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Truncate the Fock space {#truncate-the-fock-space}"
msgstr "Potong ruang Fock {#truncate-the-fock-space}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A mode that is kept to $d = n_\\text{max} + 1$ levels, where $n_\\text{max}$ is its `max_occupation`, no longer obeys the canonical commutation relation. Writing $\\bar{b}$ for the annihilation operator truncated to those levels,\n"
msgstr "Sebuah mode yang dipertahankan sampai $d = n_\\text{max} + 1$ level, dengan $n_\\text{max}$ adalah `max_occupation`-nya, tidak lagi memenuhi relasi komutasi kanonik. Dengan menulis $\\bar{b}$ untuk operator annihilation yang dipotong ke level-level itu,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"[\\bar{b}, \\bar{b}^\\dagger] = 1 - d \\, \\lvert d-1 \\rangle\\langle d-1 \\rvert \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"[\\bar{b}, \\bar{b}^\\dagger] = 1 - d \\, \\lvert d-1 \\rangle\\langle d-1 \\rvert \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "so the relation holds on every level except the highest <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id4). You can see this by mapping the commutator of the two ladder operators and reading its diagonal on the levels of one mode. The following helper builds the dense matrix of a mapped operator for a single mode, which is only reasonable for very small registers:\n"
msgstr "jadi relasi tersebut berlaku di setiap level kecuali yang tertinggi <span id=\"id1\" />[\\[1\\]](#id4). Kamu bisa melihatnya dengan memetakan komutator kedua operator ladder dan membaca diagonalnya pada level-level satu mode. Helper berikut membangun matriks padat dari operator yang dipetakan untuk satu mode, yang hanya masuk akal untuk register yang sangat kecil:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last entry is $1 - d$. Because this means the span of $\\{\\bar{b}^\\dagger, \\bar{b}\\}$ is not closed under the commutator, no encoding is an isomorphism of algebras. An encoding maps *states*, together with the operators that act within the truncated subspace. The following two consequences matter in practice.\n"
msgstr "Entri terakhir adalah $1 - d$. Karena ini berarti rentang $\\{\\bar{b}^\\dagger, \\bar{b}\\}$ tidak tertutup di bawah komutator, tidak ada encoding yang merupakan isomorfisme aljabar. Sebuah encoding memetakan *state*, bersama operator yang bekerja di dalam subruang terpotong. Dua konsekuensi berikut penting dalam praktik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The cutoff must bound the reachable occupation.** It is not enough to bound the occupation you start with. A beamsplitter acting on $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ populates $\\lvert 2, 0 \\rangle$ and $\\lvert 0, 2 \\rangle$, so a cutoff of one silently produces a wrong state:\n"
msgstr "**Cutoff harus membatasi okupansi yang bisa dicapai.** Tidak cukup hanya membatasi okupansi awal. Sebuah beamsplitter yang bekerja pada $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ mengisi $\\lvert 2, 0 \\rangle$ dan $\\lvert 0, 2 \\rangle$, jadi cutoff satu diam-diam menghasilkan state yang salah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With a cutoff of one, the probability of staying in $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ is one, because the two states that the dynamics would populate do not exist. With a cutoff of two, it vanishes, which is the Hong-Ou-Mandel effect. This is why `max_occupation` is a required argument that never has a default: it is a modeling decision and a convergence parameter that you are expected to sweep.\n"
msgstr "Dengan cutoff satu, probabilitas tetap di $\\lvert 1, 1 \\rangle$ adalah satu, karena dua state yang akan diisi oleh dinamika itu tidak ada. Dengan cutoff dua, probabilitasnya lenyap, yaitu efek Hong-Ou-Mandel. Inilah kenapa `max_occupation` adalah argumen wajib yang tidak pernah punya default: ini keputusan pemodelan sekaligus parameter konvergensi yang memang seharusnya kamu sapu (sweep).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Mapping does not commute with normal ordering.** The operators $b b^\\dagger$ and $b^\\dagger b + 1$ are equal before truncation, but they map to different qubit operators:\n"
msgstr "**Mapping tidak komut dengan normal ordering.** Operator $b b^\\dagger$ dan $b^\\dagger b + 1$ sama sebelum pemotongan, tapi keduanya dipetakan ke operator qubit yang berbeda:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two agree on every level but the highest. Applied to the top level, $b^\\dagger$ has nowhere to go and the amplitude is clipped, so $b b^\\dagger$ is zero there, whereas $b^\\dagger b + 1$ gives $d$. Decide once whether your Hamiltonian is defined in normal-ordered form, and map that form consistently.\n"
msgstr "Keduanya sama di setiap level kecuali yang tertinggi. Saat diterapkan pada level teratas, $b^\\dagger$ tidak punya tujuan dan amplitudonya terpotong, jadi $b b^\\dagger$ bernilai nol di situ, sedangkan $b^\\dagger b + 1$ memberi $d$. Putuskan sekali apakah Hamiltonian-mu didefinisikan dalam bentuk normal-ordered, lalu petakan bentuk itu secara konsisten.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three methods help you choose a cutoff, and all of them are lower bounds. The operator reports the largest number of creation operators that it applies to each mode within a single term, and a spec compares that with its cutoffs:\n"
msgstr "Tiga metode membantu kamu memilih cutoff, dan semuanya adalah batas bawah. Operator melaporkan jumlah terbesar operator creation yang ia terapkan pada tiap mode dalam satu suku, dan sebuah spec membandingkannya dengan cutoff-nya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A non-zero entry means the cutoff is below the bound, and the value is how far. These helpers do not know about the dynamics, so a passing check does not make a cutoff sufficient; the beamsplitter above has a bound of one yet needs a cutoff of two. They can also report a shortfall for a term that is zero on the retained levels, as $b^\\dagger b^\\dagger b b$ is for a cutoff of one.\n"
msgstr "Entri bukan nol berarti cutoff berada di bawah batas, dan nilainya adalah seberapa jauh. Helper ini tidak tahu soal dinamikanya, jadi pengecekan yang lolos tidak membuat sebuah cutoff cukup; beamsplitter di atas punya batas satu tapi butuh cutoff dua. Helper ini juga bisa melaporkan kekurangan untuk suku yang bernilai nol pada level yang dipertahankan, seperti $b^\\dagger b^\\dagger b b$ untuk cutoff satu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"level-spec-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Describe the truncation with a LevelSpec {#describe-the-truncation-with-a-levelspec}"
msgstr "Deskripsikan pemotongan dengan LevelSpec {#describe-the-truncation-with-a-levelspec}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") bundles the cutoff of every mode with the encoding, and it derives from them how many qubits each mode occupies and where its qubits start. Everything that has to agree about that (the mapper, the transpiler layout, the state preparation) is given the same spec. The encoding is a required argument, and so is the cutoff: neither has a default.\n"
msgstr "Sebuah [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") menggabungkan cutoff tiap mode dengan encoding, dan dari keduanya ia menurunkan berapa banyak qubit yang dipakai tiap mode dan di mana qubit-qubitnya dimulai. Semua yang harus sepakat soal itu (mapper, layout Transpiler, state preparation) diberi spec yang sama. Encoding adalah argumen wajib, begitu juga cutoff: keduanya tidak punya default.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The cutoff is either one integer, shared by all modes, or one integer per mode:\n"
msgstr "Cutoff bisa berupa satu bilangan bulat yang dipakai bersama oleh semua mode, atau satu bilangan bulat per mode:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A spec built from a single integer leaves the number of modes open, so you have to resolve it before asking for widths. A sequence is never broadcast, whatever its length, and it fixes the number of modes:\n"
msgstr "Spec yang dibangun dari satu bilangan bulat membiarkan jumlah mode terbuka, jadi kamu harus meresolusinya sebelum meminta lebar. Sebuah urutan tidak pernah di-broadcast, berapa pun panjangnya, dan ia menetapkan jumlah mode:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mode $m$ occupies the qubits `offsets[m]` to `offsets[m] + widths[m] - 1`, so modes with different cutoffs can take different numbers of qubits, and the offsets are the running sum of the widths. You do not need to pass the number of modes to the mapper. It takes it from the spec, or, for a spec with a single cutoff, from the operator through [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\"). The register can be wider than the modes need; the surplus qubits are idle and sit at the end:\n"
msgstr "Mode $m$ menempati qubit `offsets[m]` sampai `offsets[m] + widths[m] - 1`, jadi mode dengan cutoff berbeda bisa memakai jumlah qubit yang berbeda, dan offset adalah jumlah kumulatif dari lebar. Kamu tidak perlu memberikan jumlah mode ke mapper. Ia mengambilnya dari spec, atau, untuk spec dengan satu cutoff, dari operator lewat [`min_num_modes()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-operator#qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes \"qiskit_bosons.operators.BosonOperator.min_num_modes\"). Register boleh lebih lebar dari yang dibutuhkan mode; qubit sisanya menganggur dan berada di ujung:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An operator that acts on a mode beyond the last one of a per-mode spec is refused:\n"
msgstr "Operator yang bekerja pada mode di luar mode terakhir dari spec per-mode akan ditolak:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A few limits follow from how the encodings count qubits. Under a compact encoding, a mode with a single level (`max_occupation = 0`) takes no qubit at all, because its one level needs nothing to be told apart from another. Such a mode is allowed and does not move the qubits of the modes after it, but a spec in which every mode would take no qubit is rejected. The unary encodings hold at most 128 levels per mode, and a larger cutoff raises an error that suggests a compact encoding:\n"
msgstr "Beberapa batasan muncul dari cara encoding menghitung qubit. Di bawah encoding compact, mode dengan satu level (`max_occupation = 0`) tidak memakai qubit sama sekali, karena satu levelnya tidak butuh apa-apa untuk dibedakan dari yang lain. Mode seperti itu diperbolehkan dan tidak menggeser qubit mode-mode sesudahnya, tapi spec yang setiap modenya tidak memakai qubit akan ditolak. Encoding unary menampung paling banyak 128 level per mode, dan cutoff yang lebih besar memunculkan error yang menyarankan encoding compact:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose an encoding {#choose-an-encoding}"
msgstr "Pilih sebuah encoding {#choose-an-encoding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A [`LevelEncoding`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding\") decides which basis state of a block of qubits represents each level. There are four, and no one of them is best in general <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id5). The number of qubits per mode and the bit pattern of each level follow from the encoding:\n"
msgstr "Sebuah [`LevelEncoding`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-level-encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding\") menentukan basis state mana dari sebuah blok qubit yang mewakili tiap level. Ada empat, dan tidak ada satu pun yang terbaik secara umum <span id=\"id2\" />[\\[2\\]](#id5). Jumlah qubit per mode dan pola bit tiap level mengikuti dari encoding-nya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bit patterns are integers in which bit $q$ is the value of qubit $q$. The unary encodings spend one qubit per level and set one of them. The compact encodings spend $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ qubits and store the level number, in binary or as a Gray code in which neighboring levels differ in one bit. The string name of an encoding is accepted wherever the encoding is.\n"
msgstr "Pola bit adalah bilangan bulat di mana bit $q$ adalah nilai qubit $q$. Encoding unary memakai satu qubit per level dan menyetel salah satunya. Encoding compact memakai $\\lceil \\log_2 d \\rceil$ qubit dan menyimpan nomor level, dalam biner atau sebagai kode Gray di mana level bertetangga berbeda satu bit. Nama string dari sebuah encoding diterima di mana pun encoding-nya diterima.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The trade-off is qubits against operator weight. The compact encodings need exponentially fewer qubits, but a ladder operator connects levels whose patterns can differ in several bits, so its terms act on more qubits. The following sections look at what this costs, starting with the two unary encodings, which have identical layouts and differ only in the operator.\n"
msgstr "Trade-off-nya adalah qubit melawan bobot operator. Encoding compact membutuhkan qubit yang jauh lebih sedikit secara eksponensial, tapi operator ladder menghubungkan level yang pola-polanya bisa berbeda di beberapa bit, sehingga suku-sukunya bekerja pada lebih banyak qubit. Bagian-bagian berikut melihat berapa biayanya, dimulai dari dua encoding unary, yang tata letaknya identik dan hanya berbeda di operatornya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"unary-variants-explanation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare the two unary encodings {#compare-the-two-unary-encodings}"
msgstr "Bandingkan dua encoding unary {#compare-the-two-unary-encodings}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the unary encoding a ladder operator moves one excitation between two neighboring qubits. To write that as an operator on the whole mode, you must choose what to do with the other qubits. The two variants choose differently:\n"
msgstr "Di encoding unary, operator ladder memindahkan satu eksitasi di antara dua qubit bertetangga. Untuk menuliskannya sebagai operator pada seluruh mode, kamu harus memilih apa yang dilakukan pada qubit lainnya. Kedua varian memilih secara berbeda:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`unary_projected` puts a projector $\\lvert 0 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$ on every other qubit of the mode. That enforces the one-hot constraint in the operator itself: the term acts only if the rest of the mode is empty.\n"
msgstr "`unary_projected` menaruh proyektor $\\lvert 0 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$ pada setiap qubit lain dari mode. Itu menegakkan batasan one-hot di dalam operator itu sendiri: suku hanya bekerja kalau sisa mode kosong.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '*   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`unary_unprojected` leaves those qubits alone, so the term acts as the identity on them.\n"
msgstr "`unary_unprojected` membiarkan qubit-qubit itu apa adanya, jadi suku bekerja sebagai identitas pada qubit tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Look at a single $b^\\dagger$ at $d = 4$ under both. The mapper returns a [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), whose terms are strings of single-qubit bit terms. Here are the first four terms of each, with the qubits they act on:\n"
msgstr "Lihat satu $b^\\dagger$ pada $d = 4$ di bawah keduanya. Mapper mengembalikan [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable), yang suku-sukunya berupa string bit term single-qubit. Berikut empat suku pertama dari masing-masing, beserta qubit yang dikenai:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both have twelve terms with the same coefficients. The projected terms carry a `0` bit term on the two qubits that the unprojected terms do not mention, so each projected term touches all four qubits and each unprojected term touches two. In general a projected term touches all $d$ qubits of the mode, because it carries two factors, each $X$ or $Y$, and a projector on each other qubit.\n"
msgstr "Keduanya punya dua belas suku dengan koefisien yang sama. Suku yang diproyeksikan membawa bit term `0` pada dua qubit yang tidak disebut oleh suku yang tidak diproyeksikan, jadi setiap suku terproyeksi menyentuh keempat qubit dan setiap suku tak terproyeksi menyentuh dua. Secara umum, suku terproyeksi menyentuh semua $d$ qubit dari mode, karena ia membawa dua faktor, masing-masing $X$ atau $Y$, dan sebuah proyektor pada tiap qubit lainnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two operators are equal on the states that the encoding is meant for, the one-hot basis states (the codewords), and differ outside them. To check, take a small operator on two modes at $d = 3$ and compare the matrices on the nine codewords:\n"
msgstr "Kedua operator sama pada state yang dituju encoding-nya, yaitu basis state one-hot (codeword), dan berbeda di luarnya. Untuk mengeceknya, ambil operator kecil pada dua mode di $d = 3$ dan bandingkan matriksnya pada sembilan codeword:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both also leave the codeword subspace invariant, so a state prepared on a codeword stays on codewords. The choice matters only for states that leave that subspace, for example through noise. There the projected operator suppresses the evolution, because its projectors fail, whereas the unprojected one keeps acting. Neither behavior is a physical requirement. The unprojected operator is only defined on the one-hot subspace, so choosing it is a modeling decision and not a free optimization.\n"
msgstr "Keduanya juga membiarkan subruang codeword tetap invarian, jadi state yang disiapkan pada sebuah codeword tetap berada di codeword. Pilihan ini hanya berpengaruh untuk state yang keluar dari subruang itu, misalnya lewat noise. Di sana operator terproyeksi menekan evolusi, karena proyektornya gagal, sedangkan yang tak terproyeksi terus bekerja. Tidak ada perilaku yang merupakan persyaratan fisik. Operator tak terproyeksi hanya terdefinisi pada subruang one-hot, jadi memilihnya adalah keputusan pemodelan, bukan optimasi gratis.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "What the projectors cost is gates. Evolve a Hermitian $b^\\dagger + b$ on one mode for a short time, and count the two-qubit gates after Qiskit’s transpilation:\n"
msgstr "Harga dari proyektor adalah gate. Evolusikan $b^\\dagger + b$ yang Hermitian pada satu mode untuk waktu singkat, lalu hitung gate dua-qubit setelah transpilasi Qiskit:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The exact counts depend on how Qiskit synthesizes the evolution gate, which changes between releases, so plot them:\n"
msgstr "Jumlah persisnya bergantung pada cara Qiskit mensintesis evolution gate, yang berubah antar rilis, jadi plot saja:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![CX count against the number of levels d for the four encodings. The unary\\_projected count grows fastest, the unary\\_unprojected count grows linearly, and the Gray code is the cheapest.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/mappers-14.avif)\n"
msgstr "![CX count against the number of levels d for the four encodings. The unary\\_projected count grows fastest, the unary\\_unprojected count grows linearly, and the Gray code is the cheapest.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/mappers-14.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The unprojected count grows linearly with $d$, because each of the $d - 1$ transitions is a two-qubit rotation. The projected count grows much faster, because every term acts on all $d$ qubits. The compact encodings need fewer qubits, but the weight of their terms depends on how the bit patterns of neighboring levels differ: the Gray code, in which they differ in one bit, is the cheaper of the two compact encodings, and standard binary jumps when a carry flips several bits at once ($d = 5$). Whether a compact encoding also beats the unprojected unary one depends on $d$ and on how Qiskit synthesizes the evolution, so read the trend and not the ranking at one size.\n"
msgstr "Jumlah tak terproyeksi tumbuh secara linear terhadap $d$, karena tiap dari $d - 1$ transisi adalah rotasi dua-qubit. Jumlah terproyeksi tumbuh jauh lebih cepat, karena setiap suku bekerja pada semua $d$ qubit. Encoding compact butuh lebih sedikit qubit, tapi bobot suku-sukunya bergantung pada bagaimana pola bit level bertetangga berbeda: kode Gray, yang beda satu bit, adalah yang lebih murah dari dua encoding compact, dan biner standar melonjak saat carry membalik beberapa bit sekaligus ($d = 5$). Apakah encoding compact juga mengalahkan unary tak terproyeksi bergantung pada $d$ dan cara Qiskit mensintesis evolusinya, jadi bacalah tren-nya, bukan peringkat pada satu ukuran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The projectors also matter when you expand a mapped operator into Paulis, which [`from_sparse_observable()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp#from_sparse_observable) does by replacing each projector with a sum of two Pauli operators. A term with $k$ projectors becomes $2^k$ Pauli terms. Here is a single $b^\\dagger$ at small $d$, which is the only size at which you should try this:\n"
msgstr "Proyektor juga penting saat kamu mengembangkan operator terpetakan menjadi Pauli, yang dilakukan oleh [`from_sparse_observable()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp#from_sparse_observable) dengan mengganti tiap proyektor dengan jumlah dua operator Pauli. Suku dengan $k$ proyektor menjadi $2^k$ suku Pauli. Berikut satu $b^\\dagger$ pada $d$ kecil, yang merupakan satu-satunya ukuran di mana kamu sebaiknya mencoba ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both variants store the same number of terms, but the expansion of the projected one grows exponentially in $d$. For anything larger than a toy example, read the terms of the [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable) directly, as the listing above does, instead of converting it.\n"
msgstr "Kedua varian menyimpan jumlah suku yang sama, tapi ekspansi varian terproyeksi tumbuh secara eksponensial terhadap $d$. Untuk apa pun yang lebih besar dari contoh mainan, baca suku-suku [`SparseObservable`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparseObservable) secara langsung, seperti yang dilakukan listing di atas, daripada mengonversinya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The compact encodings cannot drop their projectors. There the zero bits are part of the level number, so removing a $\\lvert 0 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$ changes which levels a term connects, and the operator is no longer the same on the codewords. This is why only the unary encoding comes in two variants.\n"
msgstr "Encoding compact tidak bisa membuang proyektornya. Di sana bit nol adalah bagian dari nomor level, jadi menghapus $\\lvert 0 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$ mengubah level mana yang dihubungkan suku, dan operatornya tidak lagi sama pada codeword. Inilah kenapa hanya encoding unary yang punya dua varian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "A product of ladders is truncated first {#a-product-of-ladders-is-truncated-first}"
msgstr "Perkalian ladder dipotong dulu {#a-product-of-ladders-is-truncated-first}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One more design choice shows up in the cost of diagonal terms. The mapper does not map each ladder operator and multiply the results. It collects the ladder operators that a term applies to one mode, multiplies them as a $d \\times d$ matrix in the Fock basis, truncates that product once, and encodes the result <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[2\\]](#id5). A product such as the number operator $b^\\dagger b$ therefore stays diagonal:\n"
msgstr "Satu pilihan desain lagi terlihat pada biaya suku diagonal. Mapper tidak memetakan tiap operator ladder lalu mengalikan hasilnya. Ia mengumpulkan operator ladder yang diterapkan suku pada satu mode, mengalikannya sebagai matriks $d \\times d$ di basis Fock, memotong hasil kali itu sekali, dan meng-encode hasilnya <span id=\"id3\" />[\\[2\\]](#id5). Hasil kali seperti operator bilangan $b^\\dagger b$ dengan begitu tetap diagonal:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Its terms are the projectors $\\lvert 1 \\rangle\\langle 1 \\rvert$ on the qubit of each level above zero, weighted by the level number (level zero has weight zero and so has no term). A time evolution of it is a set of single-qubit rotations and needs no two-qubit gate. Multiplying the two mapped ladder operators instead gives the same operator on the codewords, but a different one outside them, with off-diagonal strings that cost gates:\n"
msgstr "Suku-sukunya adalah proyektor $\\lvert 1 \\rangle\\langle 1 \\rvert$ pada qubit tiap level di atas nol, dibobot dengan nomor level (level nol berbobot nol sehingga tidak punya suku). Evolusi waktu darinya berupa sekumpulan rotasi single-qubit dan tidak butuh gate dua-qubit. Mengalikan dua operator ladder terpetakan sebagai gantinya memberi operator yang sama pada codeword, tapi berbeda di luarnya, dengan string off-diagonal yang memakan biaya gate:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Diagonal terms such as the on-site interaction of the Bose-Hubbard model are these products, which is where this choice matters.\n"
msgstr "Suku diagonal seperti interaksi on-site pada model Bose-Hubbard adalah hasil kali semacam ini, dan di situlah pilihan ini berpengaruh.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write a custom mapper {#write-a-custom-mapper}"
msgstr "Tulis mapper kustom {#write-a-custom-mapper}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you want an encoding that the library does not provide, build it from the image of a single ladder operator. [`map_boson_action_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-map-boson-action-generators#qiskit_bosons.mappers.map_boson_action_generators \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.map_boson_action_generators\") takes a function that maps one [`BosonAction`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-action-boson-action#qiskit_bosons.operators.boson_action.BosonAction \"qiskit_bosons.operators.boson_action.BosonAction\"), a function that returns the identity, and builds the mapper of whole operators from them. It multiplies the images of the actions of each term in order, scales by the coefficient, and sums the terms. The output can be any type that supports scalar multiplication and composition.\n"
msgstr "Kalau kamu menginginkan encoding yang tidak disediakan pustaka, bangun dari citra satu operator ladder. [`map_boson_action_generators()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-map-boson-action-generators#qiskit_bosons.mappers.map_boson_action_generators \"qiskit_bosons.mappers.map_boson_action_generators\") menerima sebuah fungsi yang memetakan satu [`BosonAction`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-boson-action-boson-action#qiskit_bosons.operators.boson_action.BosonAction \"qiskit_bosons.operators.boson_action.BosonAction\"), sebuah fungsi yang mengembalikan identitas, lalu membangun mapper untuk operator utuh dari keduanya. Ia mengalikan citra aksi tiap suku secara berurutan, mengalikan dengan koefisien, dan menjumlahkan suku-sukunya. Outputnya bisa tipe apa pun yang mendukung perkalian skalar dan komposisi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As an example, take the encoding for $d = 2$ that stores a mode in one qubit. A creation operator is $\\lvert 1 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$, which is $(X - iY)/2$ in Qiskit’s convention, and an annihilation operator is its adjoint:\n"
msgstr "Sebagai contoh, ambil encoding untuk $d = 2$ yang menyimpan satu mode dalam satu qubit. Operator creation adalah $\\lvert 1 \\rangle\\langle 0 \\rvert$, yaitu $(X - iY)/2$ dalam konvensi Qiskit, dan operator annihilation adalah adjoin-nya:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This hand-written mapper multiplies the mapped ladder operators, and it agrees with the library mapper here because every mode has two levels and a qubit holds the whole mode. At larger $d$, as the previous section showed, composing the mapped ladders and truncating the product first are not the same operator outside the codewords.\n"
msgstr "Mapper tulisan tangan ini mengalikan operator ladder yang dipetakan, dan hasilnya sesuai dengan mapper pustaka di sini karena setiap mode punya dua level dan satu qubit menampung seluruh mode. Pada $d$ yang lebih besar, seperti yang ditunjukkan bagian sebelumnya, menyusun ladder terpetakan dan memotong hasil kali terlebih dahulu bukanlah operator yang sama di luar codeword.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To use such a mapper in a circuit, wrap it in a function with the signature `(operator, num_qubits) -> SparseObservable` and hand it to [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\"), which maps the operator of every [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") gate with it. The transpiler pipeline is described in [Transpile bosonic circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"
msgstr "Untuk memakai mapper seperti itu dalam Circuit, bungkus dalam fungsi dengan signature `(operator, num_qubits) -> SparseObservable` dan berikan ke [`MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-mapper-fn-evolution-synthesis#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.MapperFnEvolutionSynthesis\"), yang memetakan operator dari setiap gate [`Evolution`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-library-evolution#qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution \"qiskit_bosons.circuit.library.Evolution\") dengannya. Pipeline Transpiler dijelaskan di [Transpile Circuit bosonik](transpilation#transpilation-explanation).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two details are worth knowing. First, the qubit operator must have real coefficients, because [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) rejects an imaginary part. A Hermitian operator maps to a real one, but only once the terms that cancel have been merged. This hand-written mapper does not merge them, so a hopping term and its adjoint leave imaginary coefficients behind until you simplify the result. The library mapper merges its own result; a custom one has to do it, for example by wrapping it in [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-simplify#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify\"):\n"
msgstr "Dua detail layak diketahui. Pertama, operator qubit harus punya koefisien riil, karena [`PauliEvolutionGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.PauliEvolutionGate) menolak bagian imajiner. Operator Hermitian dipetakan ke operator riil, tapi hanya setelah suku-suku yang saling meniadakan digabungkan. Mapper tulisan tangan ini tidak menggabungkannya, jadi suku hopping dan adjoin-nya meninggalkan koefisien imajiner sampai kamu menyederhanakan hasilnya. Mapper pustaka menggabungkan hasilnya sendiri; mapper kustom harus melakukannya, misalnya dengan membungkusnya dalam [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-simplify#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify\"):\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Second, a product formula synthesizes the terms in the order it receives them, and the order a mapper produces is not guaranteed to be stable. The helpers [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-simplify#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify\") and [`group_wise()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-group-wise#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise\") wrap a mapper function to control it: `simplify` merges duplicate strings and sorts the terms into a canonical order, whereas `group_wise` maps one group of the operator at a time so that the terms of a group stay adjacent. Do not combine the two, because sorting discards the grouping. The [grouping guide](grouping#grouping-explanation) shows how to assign groups, and the [synthesis guide](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) shows how the order affects the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Kedua, product formula mensintesis suku-suku sesuai urutan yang diterimanya, dan urutan yang dihasilkan mapper tidak dijamin stabil. Helper [`simplify()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-simplify#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.simplify\") dan [`group_wise()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/transpiler-passes-synthesis-group-wise#qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise \"qiskit_bosons.transpiler.passes.synthesis.group_wise\") membungkus fungsi mapper untuk mengendalikannya: `simplify` menggabungkan string duplikat dan mengurutkan suku ke urutan kanonik, sedangkan `group_wise` memetakan satu grup operator sekali waktu sehingga suku-suku sebuah grup tetap berdekatan. Jangan gabungkan keduanya, karena pengurutan membuang pengelompokan. [Panduan pengelompokan](grouping#grouping-explanation) menunjukkan cara menetapkan grup, dan [panduan sintesis](bosonic-synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) menunjukkan bagaimana urutan memengaruhi Circuit.\n"

